      "description": "A high angle perspective of a cemetery includes a flagpole at center in a conifer tree-lined walkway, neat rows of marble grave markers and burial sections, a Superintendent's House in the rear, and parking lot to the right. Rolling open grasslands extend in the distance.\nA high angle perspective emphasizes the design characteristics of the historic landscape, with the flagpole, tree-lined walkways, neat rows of marble grave markers and burial sections, and Superintendent's House in the rear (at the original entrance). The cemetery landscape continues to be a place of solemn commemoration, and it also is a reflection of efforts to formalize memorialization on the battlefield and in the country.\nKeywords: cemetery; national cemetery; designed landscape; aerial; flagpole; Little Bighorn Battlefield",
